Z||000000||88 Fiero GT Turbo||05-19-2001||11:47 AM||||     I am looking to buy a 3.4 v6 to put into my Fiero.  I have e-mailed the Fiero factory and for a long block remanufactured he wants $1750 plus $500 for the prep work.  I was hoping to find a block and use my top half of my motor. <P>     I was hopeing that you guys could help me in locating some place alittle closer to Rhode Island.  <P>     Any information that you can give me on location and price would be great.  Thanks for all your help.<P>Later,<BR>Jack <P>88 Fiero GT Turbo<P>||||reg||5
Z||000001||Songman||05-19-2001||12:31 PM||||Click my link below and e-mail Keith. He is a member of our Fiero group and also sells engines for a living. He sells to Fiero Factory so you can buy the same engine direct and save... <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||7
Z||000002||88formula||05-19-2001||12:40 PM||||Linders Junk yard here in Worcester has two 3.4-liter Camaro engines still in the cars. They quoted me $450 for the one with 120k and $500 for one with I think 75k. There number is 508-756-5125. You could purchase these engines and rebuild them for a turbo installation.  Linders junk yard is very organized and clean.<P>Dobles Chevrolet in Manchester, NH sells the GM performance 3.4-liter Crate motor for about $1700. Their number is 800-842-9600. You can see what they sell through the GM performance website <A HREF="http://www.spoperformanceparts.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.spoperformanceparts.com</A>  <P>I have a drill guide plate that I used to drill the starter holes in my 3.4-liter engine. I can drill them for you for $25 and show you how to modify the motor mount. It's very easy.<BR><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
